但我觉得当你做出这样的小决定时，观众是能感受到的，你懂吗？

477
00:19:13.000 --> 00:19:13.680
She's great.
她太棒了。

478
00:19:13.820 --> 00:19:14.240
She is.
确实。

479
00:19:14.380 --> 00:19:18.920
She reminded me of like a second grade teacher when she was like, how frustrating for you.
当她说“你该有多沮丧啊”的时候，她让我想起了一位小学二年级的老师。

480
00:19:19.300 --> 00:19:21.540
Do we want to talk about our feelings?
我们要聊聊我们的感受吗？

481
00:19:21.800 --> 00:19:22.160
Yes.
好啊。

482
00:19:22.500 --> 00:19:25.220
We also got a fan catch from Ryan C in Mexico.
我们还收到了来自墨西哥的Ryan C发来的粉丝发现。

483
00:19:25.780 --> 00:19:28.840
He noticed that there's a hole in the wall behind Stephanie's desk.
他注意到斯蒂芬妮（Stephanie）办公桌后面的墙上有个洞。

484
00:19:28.840 --> 00:19:30.140
And there is.
确实有。

485
00:19:30.920 --> 00:19:31.680
Is there the hole?
真的有那个洞吗？

486
00:19:31.900 --> 00:19:32.040
Yeah.
是的。

487
00:19:32.160 --> 00:19:33.340
There's a hole behind the front.
前台后面有个洞。

488
00:19:33.580 --> 00:19:34.940
It's over her right shoulder.
就在她右肩上方。

489
00:19:35.260 --> 00:19:35.480
Okay.
好吧。

490
00:19:35.760 --> 00:19:37.220
He wanted to know what happened.
他想知道发生了什么。

491
00:19:37.360 --> 00:19:38.260
I don't know, Ryan.
我不知道，Ryan。

492
00:19:38.620 --> 00:19:41.460
But now every time we cut to her, I see the hole in the wall.
但现在每次镜头切到她，我都能看到墙上的那个洞。

493
00:19:41.620 --> 00:19:43.120
This is what happened to me in this episode.
这一集里我也遇到了同样的情况。

494
00:19:43.340 --> 00:19:44.080
People wrote in.
观众们写信来。

495
00:19:44.180 --> 00:19:45.140
They pointed things out.
他们指出了这些细节。

496
00:19:45.260 --> 00:19:46.540
And then you couldn't unsee them.
然后你就再也无法忽视它们了。

497
00:19:46.640 --> 00:19:46.940
Correct.
没错。

498
00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:48.080
So I'm passing that along.
所以我把这个发现转达给你们。

499
00:19:48.620 --> 00:19:51.920
There's going to be a very funny moment now between Gabe and Dwight.
现在盖博和德怀特之间会有一个非常有趣的时刻。

500
00:19:51.920 --> 00:19:56.480
As Dwight sort of takes in where Gabe sits and he says he's surrounded by shrubbery like
德怀特打量着盖博的座位，说他被灌木丛包围了，就像

501
00:19:56.480 --> 00:19:57.540
a squirrel's office.
松鼠的办公室。

502
00:19:58.040 --> 00:19:59.880
That just cracked me up.
那真是把我逗乐了。

503
00:20:00.140 --> 00:20:01.600
Gabe is going to have a talking head.
盖博会有一个单独访谈。

504
00:20:01.760 --> 00:20:04.960
We've spoke about this talking head before because it was in deleted scenes for another
我们之前谈过这个访谈，因为它出现在另一集的

505
00:20:04.960 --> 00:20:05.460
episode.
删减片段里。

506
00:20:05.620 --> 00:20:05.820
Yeah.
没错。

507
00:20:05.960 --> 00:20:10.820
But he's going to explain how often he has to fly back from Scranton to Florida and back
但他会解释他有多频繁地需要在斯克兰顿和佛罗里达之间

508
00:20:10.820 --> 00:20:11.280
and forth.
来回奔波。

509
00:20:11.280 --> 00:20:13.460
And also he has this fear of flying.
而且他还有飞行恐惧症。

510
00:20:13.680 --> 00:20:15.780
So what a better way to tackle that.
所以还有什么比这更好的解决方式呢。

511
00:20:16.360 --> 00:20:19.600
Robert is going to show up and is surprised to see Dwight.
罗伯特会出现，并对看到德怀特感到惊讶。

512
00:20:19.600 --> 00:20:21.480
And says, you know what?
然后说，你知道吗？

513
00:20:21.560 --> 00:20:22.620
He'll be with him shortly.
他很快就会来见他。

514
00:20:22.880 --> 00:20:23.840
Let me settle in.
让我先安顿一下。

515
00:20:24.160 --> 00:20:24.520
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

516
00:20:25.160 --> 00:20:30.680
There was a Robert Delita talking head where he shares his assessment of where Dwight is
有一个罗伯特·迪利塔的访谈，他在里面分享了对德怀特在

517
00:20:30.680 --> 00:20:31.760
at within the company.
公司里所处位置的评估。

518
00:20:32.000 --> 00:20:34.720
And he references the Peter Principle.
他还提到了彼得原理。

519
00:20:35.020 --> 00:20:35.480
Okay.
好的。

520
00:20:35.720 --> 00:20:35.880
Yeah.
没错。

521
00:20:35.980 --> 00:20:36.860
I'd never heard of this.
我以前从没听说过这个。

522
00:20:36.980 --> 00:20:40.140
Let's hear the clip and then I'll tell you what the Peter Principle is.
让我们听听这段剪辑，然后我再告诉你什么是彼得原理。

523
00:20:41.100 --> 00:20:45.540
There's a funny law of business known as the Peter Principle.
商业界有一条有趣的定律，被称为彼得原理。

524
00:20:45.540 --> 00:20:51.560
Now, every employee gets promoted until he reaches the level of his incompetence.
即，每一位员工都会被晋升，直到他达到他不称职的职位为止。

525
00:20:51.780 --> 00:20:57.180
Right now, Dwight, as a salesman, has reached his highest level of competence.
现在，德怀特作为一名销售员，已经达到了他能力的最高水平。

526
00:20:57.680 --> 00:21:01.700
Now, he's feeling the pull of moving up or moving on.
现在，他感受到了晋升或跳槽的诱惑。

527
00:21:01.700 --> 00:21:04.500
My job is to make sure that neither of those happens.
我的工作就是确保这两件事都不会发生。

528
00:21:05.760 --> 00:21:06.360
Wow.
哇。

529
00:21:06.620 --> 00:21:06.920
Yeah.
是啊。

530
00:21:07.460 --> 00:21:08.460
Isn't that interesting?
这难道不有趣吗？

531
00:21:08.940 --> 00:21:11.060
And I looked it up and it's a real thing.
我查了一下，这是真实存在的。

532
00:21:11.260 --> 00:21:14.600
It's a real sort of theory within business, the Peter Principle.
这是商业领域中一种真实的理论，彼得原理。

533
00:21:14.820 --> 00:21:21.540
It's this paradoxical idea that competent employees will continue to be promoted, but at some point
这是一种自相矛盾的观点，即称职的员工会不断得到晋升，但在某个时刻，

534
00:21:21.540 --> 00:21:25.560
will be promoted into positions for which they are, in fact, incompetent.
他们会被晋升到他们实际上无法胜任的职位上。

535
00:21:25.680 --> 00:21:29.440
And then they will remain in those positions because they don't do them well.
然后他们就会一直留在这些职位上，因为他们做不好这些工作。

536
00:21:29.440 --> 00:21:34.200
Wait, so you get to keep moving up and doing well and doing well and doing well,
等等，所以你一直晋升，表现得很好，很好，很好，

537
00:21:34.320 --> 00:21:37.400
but then the job you end up in is one you can't do well.
但最终你得到的职位却是你无法胜任的。

538
00:21:37.520 --> 00:21:39.360
Is one that you weren't qualified to do.
是一个你没有资格胜任的职位。

539
00:21:39.620 --> 00:21:43.520
Which you only find out once you get the position, but you can't be demoted.
你只有在得到这个职位后才会发现，但你又不能被降职。

540
00:21:43.860 --> 00:21:48.420
So then you just stay in this role that you aren't really fit for.
所以你就一直待在这个你并不真正适合的角色里。

541
00:21:48.680 --> 00:21:50.280
Wow, that is blowing my mind.
哇，这真是让我大开眼界。

542
00:21:50.620 --> 00:21:50.900
Yeah.
是啊。

543
00:21:51.240 --> 00:21:56.400
So sometimes I feel like if you run into someone who's in a position that they seem totally out
所以有时我觉得，如果你遇到一个看起来完全

544
00:21:56.400 --> 00:21:58.640
of their depth and you're like, how did they get this job?
无法胜任当前职位的人，你会想，他们是怎么得到这份工作的？

545
00:21:58.640 --> 00:22:00.820
Maybe they just got promoted into it.
也许他们只是被晋升到了这个位置。

546
00:22:00.840 --> 00:22:03.200
Yeah, they were really good at all the other jobs that led up to it.
没错，他们在之前所有导致晋升的工作中都表现得非常好。

547
00:22:03.280 --> 00:22:04.940
Yeah, it's called the Peter Principle.
是的，这就叫彼得原理。

548
00:22:05.120 --> 00:22:07.820
Oh, I feel like I know some Peter Principles.
哦，我觉得我认识一些彼得原理的例子。

549
00:22:08.880 --> 00:22:09.520
I do.
我也是。

550
00:22:10.100 --> 00:22:11.580
I've come across some of those.
我遇到过一些这样的人。

551
00:22:11.820 --> 00:22:12.480
I know.
我知道。

552
00:22:13.080 --> 00:22:14.400
Am I a Peter Principle?
我是彼得原理的受害者吗？

553
00:22:14.660 --> 00:22:15.100
No.
不是。

554
00:22:15.720 --> 00:22:16.460
At what?
在什么方面？

555
00:22:17.280 --> 00:22:18.020
I don't know.
我不知道。

556
00:22:18.100 --> 00:22:19.280
That's what I'm asking myself.
这也是我在问自己的问题。

557
00:22:19.540 --> 00:22:24.220
I'm sure I've Peter Principled sometime in my life where I've gotten some job and then
我肯定我这辈子也经历过彼得原理，就是得到了一份工作，然后

558
00:22:24.220 --> 00:22:25.300
I was ill-equipped.
我却无法胜任。

559
00:22:26.040 --> 00:22:27.700
Oh, I mean, for sure.
噢，我的意思是，肯定的。

560
00:22:27.700 --> 00:22:32.780
I mean, there's been a few jobs I had where really I should have just been like a spokesperson
我是说，我做过几份工作，其实我本该只当个发言人，

561
00:22:32.780 --> 00:22:36.800
and then I got promoted to where I actually had to use the skill sets of things I talked
结果我被提拔到了需要实际运用我所谈论的那些技能的岗位，

562
00:22:36.800 --> 00:22:38.360
about that I couldn't really implement.
而我根本无法执行。

563
00:22:40.540 --> 00:22:41.600
Well, I loved that.
嗯，我喜欢那个。

564
00:22:41.740 --> 00:22:42.700
That was very interesting.
那非常有意思。

565
00:22:43.140 --> 00:22:48.280
Back in Scranton, Andy is going to approach Oscar and he's hoping that Oscar can make a
在斯克兰顿，安迪打算去找奥斯卡，他希望奥斯卡能制造一个

566
00:22:48.280 --> 00:22:49.260
little rounding error.
小小的四舍五入误差。

567
00:22:49.520 --> 00:22:55.200
He wants Oscar to basically cook the books and cover up the fact that he's $830 short this
他想让奥斯卡基本上做假账，掩盖他本季度亏空了830美元的事实。

568
00:22:55.200 --> 00:22:55.540
quarter.
本季度。

569
00:22:55.800 --> 00:22:56.560
But you know what?
但你知道吗？

570
00:22:56.620 --> 00:23:01.240
Oscar can't cook the books for Andy today because he's got to get to Triviacalypse.
奥斯卡今天没法帮安迪做假账，因为他得去参加“琐事大灾难”竞赛。

571
00:23:01.640 --> 00:23:02.660
That's a mouthful.
这名字真拗口。

572
00:23:02.940 --> 00:23:03.280
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

573
00:23:03.640 --> 00:23:04.740
That's what she said.
她就是这么说的。

574
00:23:05.260 --> 00:23:06.480
Kevin offers to do it.
凯文主动提出帮忙。

575
00:23:06.600 --> 00:23:08.060
Kevin's happy to make a rounding error.
凯文很乐意制造四舍五入误差。

576
00:23:08.180 --> 00:23:09.500
He does it all the time, probably.
他可能经常这么干。

577
00:23:09.940 --> 00:23:16.120
This is when Andy is going to find out that the prize for Triviacalypse is $1,000.
就在这时，安迪发现“琐事大灾难”的奖金是1000美元。

578
00:23:16.120 --> 00:23:16.860
$1,000?
1000美元？

579
00:23:17.060 --> 00:23:19.000
That's a big prize.
那可是笔大奖。

580
00:23:19.360 --> 00:23:20.700
This gives Andy an idea.
这让安迪产生了一个想法。

581
00:23:20.940 --> 00:23:21.220
It does.
确实。

582
00:23:21.380 --> 00:23:24.440
I mean, Steve Healy only got $25 at the bar when he won.
我是说，史蒂夫·希利在酒吧赢的时候才拿到25美元。

583
00:23:24.560 --> 00:23:24.980
I know.
我知道。

584
00:23:25.440 --> 00:23:26.040
$1,000.
1000美元。

585
00:23:26.900 --> 00:23:28.920
Well, Andy now sees his opportunity.
好吧，安迪现在看到了机会。

586
00:23:29.220 --> 00:23:29.540
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

587
00:23:29.700 --> 00:23:32.420
He's going to try to get a group together to go to Trivia Night.
他打算组个队去参加琐事之夜。

588
00:23:32.500 --> 00:23:35.360
So he's talking to Jim and Daryl in his office and they're all in.
所以他在办公室里和吉姆、达里尔商量，他们都加入了。

589
00:23:35.560 --> 00:23:39.540
So there were two things about this episode that caused a stir with fans.
这一集里有两件事引起了粉丝们的骚动。

590
00:23:39.800 --> 00:23:40.000
Oh, okay.
噢，好吧。

591
00:23:40.000 --> 00:23:46.860
One actually required NBC to make a press release responding to the comments they received.
其中一件事甚至需要NBC发布新闻稿来回应他们收到的评论。

592
00:23:47.400 --> 00:23:48.240
That's later.
那是后话了。

593
00:23:48.600 --> 00:23:49.540
I'll save that.
我先留着不说。

594
00:23:50.600 --> 00:23:57.440
But the other one was the fact that Jim agrees to go to Philadelphia without any concern for his wife
但另一件事是吉姆竟然同意去费城，完全不顾家里还有妻子

595
00:23:57.440 --> 00:23:59.740
and their newborn child at home.
和刚出生的孩子。

596
00:24:00.740 --> 00:24:01.960
Can't wait to get out.
迫不及待想离开。

597
00:24:02.280 --> 00:24:04.300
There was so much mail about it.
关于这件事的邮件多得不得了。

598
00:24:04.420 --> 00:24:05.900
For example, I grabbed this one.
比如，我抓取了这一封。

599
00:24:06.020 --> 00:24:07.420
This is like when the episode aired.
这就像是这一集播出的时候收到的。

600
00:24:07.500 --> 00:24:09.380
I found this on officetelly.com.
我在officetelly.com上找到的。

601
00:24:09.380 --> 00:24:10.660
Robert wrote, quote,
罗伯特写道，引用如下：

602
00:24:11.360 --> 00:24:14.020
I just can't let go that Pam's ignored again.
我实在无法接受帕姆再次被忽视。

603
00:24:14.340 --> 00:24:18.020
Even if Jenna isn't seen or heard, which I get, I have no problem with,
即使珍娜没露面也没台词，我理解，我没意见，

604
00:24:18.500 --> 00:24:21.340
Jim should still acknowledge Pam's existence.
吉姆也应该承认帕姆的存在。

605
00:24:21.820 --> 00:24:25.660
Driving off to Philly without even a thought to his wife, an infant son,
开车去费城，却连想都没想他的妻子、刚出生的儿子

606
00:24:25.820 --> 00:24:28.300
and toddler daughter defies belief to me.
和蹒跚学步的女儿，这让我无法相信。

607
00:24:28.880 --> 00:24:30.480
Many letters of that nature.
有很多这类信件。

608
00:24:30.820 --> 00:24:32.960
So when I was rereading Clicks,
所以当我重读《点击》时，

609
00:24:33.180 --> 00:24:36.500
there's a storyline where everyone came to Jim and Pam's house.
里面有个情节是大家都去了吉姆和帕姆家。

610
00:24:36.740 --> 00:24:37.300
Yes.
是的。

611
00:24:37.300 --> 00:24:41.240
One of the things that I really liked was that Pam was mentioned.
我真的很喜欢的一点是，帕姆被提到了。

612
00:24:41.540 --> 00:24:42.940
The new baby was mentioned.
新生的宝宝也被提到了。

613
00:24:43.540 --> 00:24:45.880
And by the way, also in that script,
顺便说一下，在那份剧本里，

614
00:24:46.060 --> 00:24:49.940
it was revealed that Pam is the person who told Jim to invite Kathy.
还揭示了是帕姆让吉姆邀请凯西的。

615
00:24:50.500 --> 00:24:55.940
Because Pam suspected that Kathy might have a hard time fitting in with the group,
因为帕姆担心凯西可能很难融入大家，

616
00:24:55.940 --> 00:24:57.820
and she wanted her to be comfortable.
她想让凯西感到自在。

617
00:24:58.780 --> 00:25:00.860
I thought that was very interesting.
我觉得这非常有意思。

618
00:25:01.300 --> 00:25:04.960
But all of it got cut, you know, when the episode changed.
但当剧集改动后，这些内容全被删掉了。

619
00:25:05.120 --> 00:25:10.480
And Steve Healy actually said he wished that that reference to Pam back at home,
史蒂夫·希利其实说过，他希望有提到帕姆在家的那段内容，

620
00:25:10.640 --> 00:25:14.680
he actually said he thought this episode would have been better with more Pam and Angela.
他甚至说他觉得如果这一集里有更多帕姆和安吉拉的戏份会更好。

621
00:25:15.020 --> 00:25:16.160
Oh, well, thank you.
噢，好吧，谢谢你。

622
00:25:16.160 --> 00:25:18.700
He said he's not just saying that because he's on our podcaSt.
他说他这么说不仅仅是因为他在我们的播客里。

623
00:25:19.120 --> 00:25:20.900
Even if you are, Steve, thank you.
就算你是客套，史蒂夫，也谢谢你。

624
00:25:22.380 --> 00:25:28.200
But that was a big controversy that Jim seemed to have zero probleMs.
但那确实是个大争议，吉姆似乎对此毫无压力。

625
00:25:28.360 --> 00:25:29.100
No, all an ass.
没错，简直是个混蛋。

626
00:25:29.180 --> 00:25:32.180
Made the decision to go prior to speaking with his wife at home.
在没跟家里的妻子商量之前就做了决定。

627
00:25:32.180 --> 00:25:36.820
I wonder if I found a little scuttlebutt thing as well.
我想知道我是不是也发现了一点小道消息。

628
00:25:37.000 --> 00:25:38.460
I wonder if it's our same scuttlebutt.
不知道是不是我们说的是同一个小道消息。

629
00:25:38.460 --> 00:25:40.000
It happens later in the episode.
那是在这一集后面发生的。

630
00:25:40.120 --> 00:25:40.620
That's right.
没错。

631
00:25:40.840 --> 00:25:41.460
Okay, all right.
好的，没问题。

632
00:25:41.600 --> 00:25:42.240
Let's wait.
我们等等看。

633
00:25:42.420 --> 00:25:43.660
We'll see if we can surprise each other.
看看我们能不能给对方一个惊喜。

634
00:25:43.880 --> 00:25:44.060
Okay.
好的。

635
