我们要了解一下各队的排名情况。

1127
00:44:22.120 --> 00:44:25.260
The host is going to give the teams in order of their points.
主持人会按分数高低依次宣布各队。

1128
00:44:25.640 --> 00:44:30.780
And as he announces each team, you get to see a shot of that team.
每宣布一个队伍，你就能看到那个队伍的镜头。

1129
00:44:31.140 --> 00:44:32.580
Oh, it is the same.
哦，是一样的。

1130
00:44:32.760 --> 00:44:33.580
It is the same.
确实是一样的。

1131
00:44:33.600 --> 00:44:33.940
It is?
是吗？

1132
00:44:34.040 --> 00:44:34.540
Is this about a picture?
这是关于一张照片吗？

1133
00:44:34.720 --> 00:44:36.120
Is this about someone on a team?
这是关于队里的某个人吗？

1134
00:44:36.340 --> 00:44:36.780
Yes.
是的。

1135
00:44:36.940 --> 00:44:40.080
There is a moment where we cut to the Quirinstein Bears.
有一个镜头切到了奎林斯坦熊队。

1136
00:44:40.080 --> 00:44:42.680
This is where all the guys act like bears.
那是所有队员都在模仿熊的样子。

1137
00:44:43.000 --> 00:44:49.140
The third guy from the left, wearing a green plaid shirt, set off a fan reaction so big
左起第三个人，穿着一件绿色格子衬衫，引发了巨大的粉丝反响，

1138
00:44:49.140 --> 00:44:54.880
that NBC had to make a press release because people thought that this man was Steve Carell
以至于NBC不得不发布新闻稿，因为人们认为这个人是史蒂夫·卡瑞尔

1139
00:44:54.880 --> 00:44:56.380
in disguise.
乔装打扮的。

1140
00:44:56.700 --> 00:44:56.880
Yep.
没错。

1141
00:44:57.040 --> 00:44:59.080
Making a cameo on the episode.
在这一集中客串。

1142
00:44:59.340 --> 00:45:01.600
Sam, Cassie, I have a picture.
萨姆，卡西，我有一张照片。

1143
00:45:01.920 --> 00:45:05.880
Yes, fans thought this was an uncredited cameo by Steve.
是的，粉丝们以为这是史蒂夫未署名的客串。

1144
00:45:06.060 --> 00:45:06.680
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1145
00:45:08.120 --> 00:45:09.420
It looks like Robin WilliaMs.
看起来像罗宾·威廉姆斯。

1146
00:45:12.320 --> 00:45:16.760
We will put a picture up in Office Ladies Pod because for the third time in this episode,
我们会把照片发在《办公室女士》播客里，因为这是本集中第三次，

1147
00:45:16.920 --> 00:45:20.240
once a fan pointed something out to me, I became obsessed with it.
一旦有粉丝向我指出某件事，我就变得对此着迷了。

1148
00:45:20.720 --> 00:45:22.640
It was such a crazy thing.
这真是太疯狂了。

1149
00:45:22.780 --> 00:45:23.620
Did you read about it?
你读过关于它的报道吗？

1150
00:45:23.640 --> 00:45:24.760
I did read about it.
我确实读过。

1151
00:45:24.880 --> 00:45:29.240
And sorry, the way you set it up, I thought maybe the Quirinstein Bears had cheated or something.
抱歉，因为你们的设置方式，我还以为是“奎林斯坦熊”队作弊了什么的。

1152
00:45:29.700 --> 00:45:31.340
Or the math was wrong.
或者是算错分了。

1153
00:45:31.420 --> 00:45:34.060
And then people were like, they could be in the top three or whatever.
然后大家就说，他们可能会进前三名之类的。

1154
00:45:34.260 --> 00:45:36.060
But yes, I did read about this.
不过确实，我读到过这件事。

1155
00:45:36.060 --> 00:45:38.500
There was a whole scuttlebutt after the episode aired.
那集播出后，到处都在传流言蜚语。

1156
00:45:38.720 --> 00:45:42.260
People were all over the message boards thinking they spotted Steve.
大家都在留言板上讨论，觉得他们发现了史蒂夫。

1157
00:45:42.740 --> 00:45:48.620
I pulled one of the comments from Pat M who said, quote, I think it was Steve because first of all,
我找了一条Pat M的评论，他说，引用一下，我觉得那就是史蒂夫，首先，

1158
00:45:48.740 --> 00:45:51.760
it looks like him with a fake beard and fake eyebrows.
他戴着假胡子和假眉毛，看起来很像他。

1159
00:45:52.020 --> 00:45:57.980
Plus, later on the show, when they showed that table again, he's the only member of the group that isn't seen.
而且，节目后面再次展示那张桌子时，他是小组里唯一没露面的人。

1160
00:45:58.380 --> 00:46:04.620
I think this is an indication that Steve came to visit, did the cameo for one day, but didn't hang for the whole filming.
我觉得这说明史蒂夫来探班了，客串了一天，但没有参与全程拍摄。

1161
00:46:04.620 --> 00:46:06.340
This was the conspiracy.
这就是那个阴谋论。

1162
00:46:06.680 --> 00:46:15.500
I love that in this scenario, Steve comes to the set, makes the effort to come, but then dons a fake beard and eyebrows?
我喜欢这个设想，史蒂夫大老远跑来片场，结果是为了戴上假胡子和假眉毛？

1163
00:46:15.880 --> 00:46:16.220
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1164
00:46:16.700 --> 00:46:17.900
This is a lot of effort.
这真是费了老劲了。

1165
00:46:18.080 --> 00:46:21.580
To sit in and just act like a bear for one shot.
就为了坐那儿演一回熊，只拍一个镜头。

1166
00:46:21.740 --> 00:46:23.460
And then he's like, that was fun.
然后他就说，真好玩。

1167
00:46:23.580 --> 00:46:24.240
I'm out of here.
我先撤了。

1168
00:46:24.480 --> 00:46:26.220
I really wish he would have now.
我现在真希望他当时真的这么做了。

1169
00:46:26.220 --> 00:46:34.240
Well, this really blew up so much so that NBC gave a quote to the Washington Post saying, it was not Steve Carell.
好吧，这件事闹得沸沸扬扬，以至于NBC不得不向《华盛顿邮报》发表声明说，那不是史蒂夫·卡瑞尔。

1170
00:46:35.640 --> 00:46:37.920
They had to, like, announce it.
他们居然还得专门发个声明。

1171
00:46:38.100 --> 00:46:38.880
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1172
00:46:39.140 --> 00:46:40.160
That is so funny.
太搞笑了。

1173
00:46:40.640 --> 00:46:45.440
Well, you know, when they list the top three teams, I became very curious about what the other teams were.
嗯，你知道，当他们列出前三名队伍时，我很好奇其他队伍是什么。

1174
00:46:45.520 --> 00:46:47.040
There's a lot of other teaMs.
还有很多其他队伍呢。

1175
00:46:47.300 --> 00:46:48.540
Do they have names?
他们有名字吗？

1176
00:46:48.880 --> 00:46:54.200
I went to the shooting draft because I figured this was something the writers would have had a lot of fun with.
我查了拍摄剧本，因为我觉得编剧们肯定会在这上面玩得很开心。

1177
00:46:54.200 --> 00:46:56.540
And there are lots of other team names.
确实还有很多其他的队名。

1178
00:46:56.740 --> 00:46:57.580
Oh, let's hear them.
哦，快念来听听。

1179
00:46:57.800 --> 00:46:58.160
Yes.
好的。

1180
00:46:58.380 --> 00:47:03.480
In the script, the trivia host had a whole rundown of all the scores.
在剧本里，问答环节的主持人有一大段关于所有分数的总结。

1181
00:47:03.560 --> 00:47:04.760
It was a bigger speech.
那是一段更长的台词。

1182
00:47:04.920 --> 00:47:05.260
Oh.
哦。

1183
00:47:05.400 --> 00:47:07.020
And this is what he would have said.
这是他原本要说的内容。

1184
00:47:07.680 --> 00:47:09.520
The Querenstein Bears was seven.
“奎林斯坦熊”队七分。

1185
00:47:10.000 --> 00:47:14.520
Joey Trivia-ani, get it, was seven.
“乔伊·问答尼”队，懂吗，七分。

1186
00:47:14.840 --> 00:47:17.460
The Impish Impresarios with three.
“顽皮的经纪人”队三分。

1187
00:47:17.880 --> 00:47:20.140
Two Broke Dorks with six.
“两个破产书呆子”队六分。

1188
00:47:20.480 --> 00:47:24.000
Late Onset Bieber Fever with five.
“迟来的比伯热”队五分。

1189
00:47:24.940 --> 00:47:26.880
Dunder Mifflin A-Team with four.
“邓德·米福林A队”四分。

1190
00:47:27.180 --> 00:47:28.780
DM Backup Team with three.
“邓德·米福林后备队”三分。

1191
00:47:29.440 --> 00:47:32.020
Jason Sogakis, zero.
“杰森·索加基斯”队零分。

1192
00:47:32.820 --> 00:47:33.020
Oh.
哦。

1193
00:47:33.380 --> 00:47:34.480
Einstein's with eight.
“爱因斯坦”队八分。

1194
00:47:34.660 --> 00:47:37.040
And The Ladies Gaga with five.
还有“嘎嘎女士”队五分。

1195
00:47:37.420 --> 00:47:37.840
Ah.
啊。

1196
00:47:38.460 --> 00:47:39.140
All right.
好吧。

1197
00:47:39.140 --> 00:47:41.900
We got a fan question from Alexa P.
我们收到一个来自纽约州欧申赛德的Alexa P.的粉丝提问，她说，

1198
00:47:42.020 --> 00:47:43.560
in Oceanside, New York, who said,
嗨，珍娜和安吉拉。

1199
00:47:43.780 --> 00:47:44.620
Hi, Jenna and Angela.
我今年15岁，从《办公室女士》开播起我就一直在听。

1200
00:47:44.800 --> 00:47:48.720
I am 15 years old and I've been listening to Office Ladies pretty much since it started.
我今年15岁，从《办公室女士》开播起我就一直在听。

1201
00:47:49.140 --> 00:47:54.040
For this episode, I have always wondered why isn't Kelly on the Dunder Mifflin A-Team?
关于这一集，我一直很纳闷，为什么凯莉不在邓德·米夫林的王牌小队里？

1202
00:47:54.200 --> 00:48:01.340
When she clearly knows more about pop culture than anyone in the office, I feel like she would be my first choice to have on my team for a trivia night.
她明明比办公室里的任何人都更了解流行文化，我觉得如果我要组队参加知识竞赛，她会是我的首选。

1203
00:48:01.880 --> 00:48:02.220
Same.
我也是。

1204
00:48:02.540 --> 00:48:03.920
Alexa, I agree with you.
亚历克莎，我同意你的看法。

1205
00:48:04.000 --> 00:48:05.740
And this is exactly what Andy is discovering.
而这正是安迪所发现的。

1206
00:48:06.080 --> 00:48:11.640
He has completely underestimated the people in his office and their use in a trivia night.
他完全低估了办公室里的这些人，以及他们在知识竞赛中的作用。

1207
00:48:12.160 --> 00:48:15.500
I mean, Meredith is about to throw down some great answers.
我是说，梅雷迪思马上就要给出几个精彩的答案了。

1208
00:48:15.800 --> 00:48:17.180
Meredith is going to get one right.
梅雷迪思会答对一道题的。

1209
00:48:17.460 --> 00:48:23.460
I mean, Aaron, who Meredith calls Princess Ding Dong, is going to get Flying Jib.
我是说，亚伦——梅雷迪思管他叫“叮咚公主”——他会答出“飞帆”这个词。

1210
00:48:24.080 --> 00:48:26.740
I mean, you know, I wouldn't have got that.
我是说，你知道的，我可答不上来。

1211
00:48:27.120 --> 00:48:33.540
I did love when they get to the speed round and their, like, first team to ring in gets to answer.
我很喜欢他们进入快问快答环节的时候，第一支抢答的队伍就能回答。

1212
00:48:33.820 --> 00:48:37.100
And so Aaron rings in first and she's like, guys, I did my part.
然后亚伦抢到了，她说，伙计们，我尽力了。

1213
00:48:37.200 --> 00:48:37.920
What's the answer?
答案是什么？

1214
00:48:38.260 --> 00:48:38.310
I don't know.
我不知道。

1215
00:48:38.420 --> 00:48:39.520
That was a very funny joke.
那个笑话真好笑。

1216
00:48:39.700 --> 00:48:39.880
Yeah.
是啊。

1217
00:48:40.360 --> 00:48:45.820
Well, I think we should head back to Florida because Dwight is going to arrive at Robert's condo.
好吧，我觉得我们该回到佛罗里达了，因为德怀特要去罗伯特的公寓了。

1218
00:48:46.380 --> 00:48:50.100
This was an apartment complex in North Hollywood that was very close to the federal.
这是一个位于北好莱坞的公寓大楼，离联邦大楼很近。

1219
00:48:50.100 --> 00:48:54.180
Steve Burgess told me we shot at the federal during the day one day.
史蒂夫·伯吉斯告诉我，有一天我们白天在联邦大楼拍摄。

1220
00:48:54.360 --> 00:48:57.400
And then after we finished, we moved over to this condo complex.
拍完之后，我们就转场到了这个公寓大楼。

1221
00:48:58.360 --> 00:48:58.480
Yeah.
是啊。

1222
00:48:58.680 --> 00:49:05.600
Dwight and Gabe are going to arrive and Robert California is having a wrestling lesson, I guess.
德怀特和盖博要到了，而罗伯特·加州正在上摔跤课，我想是这样。

1223
00:49:06.060 --> 00:49:06.460
Yeah.
是啊。

1224
00:49:06.700 --> 00:49:08.360
A wrestling workout.
一次摔跤训练。

1225
00:49:08.680 --> 00:49:08.840
Yeah.
是啊。

1226
00:49:09.020 --> 00:49:12.100
With Stu, who was played by Peter Gannon.
和斯图一起，由彼得·甘农饰演。

1227
00:49:12.600 --> 00:49:15.620
I wanted to know, is this person a real wrestler?
我想知道，这个人是真正的摔跤手吗？

1228
00:49:15.960 --> 00:49:16.240
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1229
00:49:16.400 --> 00:49:18.360
You know, you get cast in a role.
你知道的，你被选入一个角色。

1230
00:49:18.780 --> 00:49:18.940
Yeah.
是啊。

1231
00:49:18.940 --> 00:49:22.020
And all he does is, like, wrestle real hard.
而他所做的就是，非常卖力地摔跤。

1232
00:49:22.280 --> 00:49:24.060
I was like, what's the story?
我当时就在想，这是什么情况？

1233
00:49:24.260 --> 00:49:26.000
I mean, he looked like he knew what he was doing.
我是说，他看起来确实知道自己在做什么。

1234
00:49:26.160 --> 00:49:34.560
Also, there's nothing funnier to me than what Robert looked like because he was at first kind of, like, he looked like a turtle on his back.
另外，对我来说，没有什么比罗伯特当时的样子更滑稽的了，因为起初他看起来就像一只四脚朝天的乌龟。

1235
00:49:34.700 --> 00:49:34.860
Yeah.
是啊。

1236
00:49:34.860 --> 00:49:38.360
You know, he was trying to, like, flip the other guy over and flailing about.
你知道，他试图把对方翻过来，在那儿乱挥乱舞。

1237
00:49:38.620 --> 00:49:40.760
And that's a very small space, you guys.
而且那是一个非常狭小的空间，伙计们。

1238
00:49:40.960 --> 00:49:46.900
Imagine watching two grown men wrestling as hard as they can but just, like, one foot in front of you.
想象一下，看着两个成年男人在离你只有一英尺远的地方拼命摔跤。

1239
00:49:46.900 --> 00:49:50.480
Yeah, like, between a couch and a coffee table they've moved.
是啊，就在他们挪开的沙发和咖啡桌之间。

1240
00:49:50.480 --> 00:49:56.440
Well, I found Peter Gannon's resume, and it does not look like he is a wrestler.
好吧，我找到了彼得·甘农的简历，看起来他并不是摔跤手。

1241
00:49:56.440 --> 00:50:07.920
He listed many special skills, which were martial arts, taekwondo, boxing, scuba diving, horseback riding, golf, baseball, skiing, both water and snow.
他列出了许多特殊技能，包括武术、跆拳道、拳击、水肺潜水、骑马、高尔夫、棒球、滑雪（水上和雪地）。

1242
00:50:07.920 --> 00:50:12.040
So I reached out to Steve Burgess, and Steve Burgess says, no.
所以我联系了史蒂夫·伯吉斯，史蒂夫·伯吉斯说，不是。

1243
00:50:12.360 --> 00:50:20.440
He is an actor they hired, and both Peter and James met with our stunt coordinator, Tom DeWire, and they just spent the morning wrestling.
他是一位被雇佣的演员，彼得和詹姆斯都见了我们的特技协调员汤姆·德怀尔，他们花了一上午时间练习摔跤。

1244
00:50:20.780 --> 00:50:25.500
And they came up with this wrestling choreography to make sure everyone would be safe in the scene.
他们设计了这套摔跤动作，以确保每个人在拍摄现场都是安全的。

1245
00:50:25.760 --> 00:50:27.040
That just blew my mind.
这简直让我大开眼界。

1246
00:50:27.220 --> 00:50:28.140
I don't know why.
我不知道为什么。

1247
00:50:28.140 --> 00:50:28.800
Yeah.
是啊。

1248
00:50:29.020 --> 00:50:29.960
What a crazy job to get.
这工作真疯狂。

1249
00:50:30.020 --> 00:50:30.400
I know.
我知道。

1250
00:50:30.600 --> 00:50:31.360
What'd you do today?
你今天做了什么？

1251
00:50:31.560 --> 00:50:33.780
I wrestled James Spader for most of the morning.
我整个上午都在和詹姆斯·斯派德摔跤。

1252
00:50:33.800 --> 00:50:36.360
I didn't have any lines, but that was my job.
我没有台词，但那就是我的工作。

1253
00:50:36.680 --> 00:50:38.200
Well, I have a question for you.
好吧，我有个问题要问你。

1254
00:50:38.320 --> 00:50:38.600
Yes.
好的。

1255
00:50:38.800 --> 00:50:39.840
What happened to Gabe?
盖博去哪了？

1256
00:50:40.200 --> 00:50:41.000
What do you mean?
你什么意思？

1257
00:50:41.240 --> 00:50:42.940
I mean, Gabe walked in with Dwight.
我是说，盖博是和德怀特一起进来的。

1258
00:50:43.600 --> 00:50:44.160
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

1259
00:50:44.160 --> 00:50:46.380
He said, yay, while they were wrestling.
他们在摔跤的时候，他说了一句“耶”。

1260
00:50:46.600 --> 00:50:46.920
What happened?
后来怎么了？

1261
00:50:46.920 --> 00:50:48.280
And then we never see him again.
然后我们就再也没见过他了。

1262
00:50:48.920 --> 00:50:49.900
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1263
00:50:49.900 --> 00:50:50.860
You're so right.
你说得太对了。

1264
00:50:50.860 --> 00:50:52.340
I didn't even notice that.
我甚至都没注意到这一点。

1265
00:50:52.900 --> 00:50:58.660
Well, here is what I got obsessed with in this scene, and I'm glad I did because it really pays off.
好吧，这一幕里让我着迷的地方是这个，我很高兴我注意到了，因为它真的很值得。

1266
00:50:58.940 --> 00:51:09.720
When Robert is done wrestling, he offers Dwight an Oreo from a platter of Oreos because he says they haven't really improved on the Oreo, have they?
当罗伯特摔跤结束后，他从一盘奥利奥里拿出一个递给德怀特，因为他说奥利奥并没有真正改进过，不是吗？

1267
00:51:10.180 --> 00:51:11.900
I did a deep dive on Oreos.
我深入研究了一下奥利奥。

1268
00:51:12.080 --> 00:51:15.480
I love that he brought them out on a platter, and I love that you are doing a deep dive.
